==Information==
===Format===
*Originally scheduled to take place from September 24<sup>th</sup> - October 29<sup>th</sup>, the event was delayed until October 26<sup>th</sup> - November 3<sup>rd</sup><ref name="delay 1">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/OW_Esports_Asia/status/2102322018464956444|title=OWCS Pacific Stage 3 | Schedule Update|author=[[OW Esports Asia]]|date=2026-09-22}}</ref>, with a second delay from that date to November 4<sup>th</sup> - 9<sup>th</sup>.<ref name="delay 2">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/OW_Esports_Asia/status/2113510983599898944|title=OWCS Pacific Stage 3 Schedule Update|author=[[OW Esports Asia]]|date=2026-10-23}}</ref>
*'''Regular Season:''' ''November 4<sup>th</sup> - November 8<sup>th</sup>''
**Round Robin 
**All matches are {{Ft|3}}
**{{Bgcolortext|up|Top 4 teams}} advance to '''Regional Playoffs'''
*'''Regional Playoffs:''' ''November 9<sup>th</sup>''
**Single elimination bracket
**All matches ''(excl. Grand Finals)'' are {{Ft|3}}
**Grand Finals are {{Ft|4}}
**{{Bgcolortext|up|Top team}} advances to {{LeagueIconSmall/owcs/asia}} [[Overwatch_Champions_Series/2026/Asia/Stage 3|OWCS Asia Stage 3]]
*'''Hero Bans'''
**Each team bans 1 hero per map, with the ban impacting both teams
**Each ban must be from a different role than the other team's ban
**Teams can only ban a hero once per series, but may repeat a ban from the opposing team
**The higher seeded team or team that has lost the last map chooses to ban first or second

